{"id":61017,"ord":135,"n_segments":146,"prev":61016,"next":61018,"doc":{"id":"70980","title":"70980_Quinn Wilson oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Quinn Wilson","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/70980/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=70980"},"chapter":"Influences, later bands and reflections","title":"How Lefty Bates's group grew","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"Trio then drums, sax.","period":"1950s","year_from":1950,"year_to":1959,"words":139,"start":[193,6],"end":[194,6],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=70980#s61017","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[{"name":"Rhumboogie","focus":0,"city":"Chicago"}],"bands":[{"name":"Lefty Bates' band","focus":1,"leader":"Lefty Bates"},{"name":"Marl Young's band","focus":0,"leader":"Marl Young"}]},"people":[{"name":"Eddie Johnson","qid":"Q576969","n":2},{"name":"Duke Ellington","qid":"Q4030","n":1},{"name":"Lefty Bates","qid":"Q6517065","n":1},{"name":"Cliff Davis","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Marl Young","qid":"Q17319102","n":1},{"name":"Alto player","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":34,"theme_name":"Who was in the band: naming sidemen and personnel","community":60,"community_name":"Who played in the band: reciting personnel","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":193,"b":6,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Well, Lefty's band, was that piano, bass, and guitar, or drums?"},{"p":193,"b":7,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"When we first started, we started out with a trio, piano, bass, and guitar. Then we added drums. Then we added saxophone. And let me see, what did we add? Saxophone; we already had the rhythm section, with the bass, guitar, and drums. Then we added that saxophone."},{"p":193,"b":8,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Who was playing saxophone?"},{"p":193,"b":9,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"Oh, we had a lot of different saxophone players. Boy that was with Duke for a while."},{"p":193,"b":10,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"In St. Louis?"},{"p":193,"b":11,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"No, he's from Chicago."},{"p":193,"b":12,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Alto player?"},{"p":194,"b":0,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"No, played tenor."},{"p":194,"b":1,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Tenor?"},{"p":194,"b":2,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"And had --"},{"p":194,"b":3,"s":"","x":"(Recording interruption.)"},{"p":194,"b":4,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"-- Cliff Davis on sax at one time. (Inaudible)."},{"p":194,"b":5,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Is that Eddie Johnson, the tenor man?"},{"p":194,"b":6,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"No, Eddie Johnson never worked with us. I worked with Eddie Johnson with the -- Merle Young's band at the Rum Boogie, during the war."}]}